## Mandatory results and crash recovery

- Result-file path: `{{ result_file.path }}`
- Format: {{ result_file.format }}
- Typed schema/nullability: {{ result_file.schema_description }}
- Initialization: {{ result_file.initialization }}
- Durable write, locking, and deduplication: {{ result_file.durable_write_policy }}
- Start manifest and recovery: {{ result_file.start_manifest_recovery }}
- Later adjudication/promotion evidence: {{ result_file.adjudication_policy }}

The result file is the authoritative outcome ledger. Verify its schema and recovery mechanism before the first trial. Do not truncate existing results.

Persist a durable start manifest before evaluation. Append exactly one terminal result for every attempted trial, including rejected, invalid, failed, timed-out, crashed, and unknown outcomes. Record trial/candidate/chain identity, timestamps, hypothesis, changed files, parent/candidate versions, comparator identity/version, data/split, seeds, procedure, environment, evaluator, metrics/nulls, evidence, runtime/cost, violations, errors, stage outcome, decision, and rationale.
{% if leaderboard.enabled %}
Also record the incumbent artifact path/version and frozen leaderboard snapshot/hash.
{% endif %}

Reconcile unfinished attempts before starting new work. Recover failures from durable evidence; use null metrics and unknown/needs_review when outcomes cannot be recovered. Deduplicate by experiment ID under the declared write policy. Give retries new IDs linked to their prior attempts. Stop if safe logging is unavailable. Never fabricate outcomes or rewrite historical records to reflect later promotion.

