## Decisions

{{ decision_rules }}

`advance` permits only the declared next validation stage. `keep` describes artifact retention, not scientific acceptance or leaderboard promotion. `accept` requires every declared acceptance condition. Record rejection, invalidity, or uncertainty explicitly and apply the approved rollback/retention policy.

## Reporting

{{ reporting }}

Write results before reporting completion. Include trial ID, hypothesis, code/artifact version, comparator, metrics and uncertainty, constraints, validation stage, decision/rationale, runtime/cost, and evidence location. At campaign end reconcile attempt counts, decisions, best candidate, validation evidence, consumed budget, and unresolved risks against the ledger. Distinguish retained candidates from accepted improvements and, where enabled, promoted leaders.

## Stop and escalation

{{ experiment.stop_escalation }}

Stop on exhausted limits, unreliable data/evaluation/logging, protocol drift, leakage, safety-boundary violations, unresolved incumbent conflicts, or any action requiring approval. Stop when acceptance and required confirmation are complete. Preserve evidence and report the reason; do not turn a stopped or incomplete campaign into a success claim.

